   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "Late-game difficulty is non-monotonic; L99 is a wall far above L100",
   "detail": "Search effort jumps between neighbours: L98 79 nodes, L99 50035, L100 8574 (L74 122 after L72/73 ~12k; L94 225). World tier (15 ms/node) failed L99 on 3 attempts (4-min cap each) but cleared L100 in 130 s; skilled cleared L99 by a lucky tie-break yet failed L75 and L100.",
   "repro": "node qa/skill-tiers/one-stroke/bot.js world 98,99,100",
   "fix": "Order levels by solver effort in demo/gen.js (e.g. sort by nodes of a first-solution DFS) or regenerate L99 / outliers (L74, L94, L98) so that effort rises monotonically."
  },
  {
   "severity": "medium",
   "title": "Hard wall for players who do not search: casual stops at L25, clumsy at L1",
   "detail": "Casual (1-step greedy + 3 hints) cleared L1/L10/L25 with 1–3 stars and failed every attempt at L50, L75, L99, L100 (4-min caps). Clumsy cleared only L1 and failed L10 five times. Three hints reveal at most 6 cells each (index.html:620), i.e. ≤18 of 53–84 cells on later boards, so hints cannot rescue a stuck casual player.",
   "repro": "node qa/skill-tiers/one-stroke/bot.js casual 25,50",
   "fix": "Scale hints with board size (e.g. HINTS_PER_LEVEL = ceil(cells/20), index.html:328) or let a hint reveal up to the next seal regardless of length; consider an easier mid-curve (L26–49) ramp."
  },
  {
   "severity": "low",
   "title": "Starting a drag slightly off the head silently rewinds the stroke",
   "detail": "pointerdown on any earlier path cell truncates the path to it (index.html:953). A finger that lands a few px into the cell before the head (common with 37 px cells on 9-wide boards) deletes the head cell; clumsy/casual bots needed 33–120 corrections per level partly from this.",
   "repro": "Draw ①→3 cells, then touchStart at (head centre − 0.55·cell toward previous cell): path length drops by 1.",
   "fix": "In pointerdown, if the touch is within ~0.6 cell of the head cell prefer the head (resume drawing); only rewind on a tap (pointerup without movement) on an earlier cell."
  }
 ],
